.TH SDL_GetTextureProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetTextureProperties \- Get the properties associated with a texture.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_PropertiesID SDL_GetTextureProperties(SDL_Texture *texture);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The following read-only properties are provided by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_COLORSPACE_NUMBER :
an
.BR SDL_Colorspace
value describing the texture colorspace\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_FORMAT_NUMBER :
one of the enumerated values in
.BR SDL_PixelFormat \[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_ACCESS_NUMBER :
one of the enumerated values in
.BR SDL_TextureAccess \[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_WIDTH_NUMBER :
the width of the texture in pixels\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_HEIGHT_NUMBER :
the height of the texture in pixels\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_SDR_WHITE_POINT_FLOAT :
for HDR10 and floating point textures, this defines the value of 100% diffuse white, with higher values being displayed in the High Dynamic Range headroom\[char46] This defaults to 100 for HDR10 textures and 1\[char46]0 for other textures\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_HDR_HEADROOM_FLOAT :
for HDR10 and floating point textures, this defines the maximum dynamic range used by the content, in terms of the SDR white point\[char46] If this is defined, any values outside the range supported by the display will be scaled into the available HDR headroom, otherwise they are clipped\[char46] This defaults to 1\[char46]0 for SDR textures, 4\[char46]0 for HDR10 textures, and no default for floating point textures\[char46]
.PP
With the direct3d11 renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_D3D11_TEXTURE_POINTER :
the ID3D11Texture2D associated with the texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_D3D11_TEXTURE_U_POINTER :
the ID3D11Texture2D associated with the U plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_D3D11_TEXTURE_V_POINTER :
the ID3D11Texture2D associated with the V plane of a YUV texture
.PP
With the direct3d12 renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_D3D12_TEXTURE_POINTER :
the ID3D12Resource associated with the texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_D3D12_TEXTURE_U_POINTER :
the ID3D12Resource associated with the U plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_D3D12_TEXTURE_V_POINTER :
the ID3D12Resource associated with the V plane of a YUV texture
.PP
With the metal renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_METAL_TEXTURE_POINTER :
the MTLTexture associated with the texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_METAL_TEXTURE_UV_POINTER :
the MTLTexture associated with the UV plane of an NV12 texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_METAL_TEXTURE_U_POINTER :
the MTLTexture associated with the U plane of a YUV texture style texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_METAL_TEXTURE_V_POINTER :
the MTLTexture associated with the V plane of a YUV texture
.PP
With the vulkan renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_VULKAN_TEXTURE_NUMBER :
the VkImage associated with the texture\[char46] For NV12 style textures this is the single two plane VkImage holding both the Y and UV planes, and for YUV style textures it is the VkImage holding the Y plane\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_VULKAN_TEXTURE_UV_NUMBER :
the VkImage associated with the UV plane of an NV12 texture, if it was created with separate planes\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_VULKAN_TEXTURE_U_NUMBER :
the VkImage associated with the U plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_VULKAN_TEXTURE_V_NUMBER :
the VkImage associated with the V plane of a YUV texture
.PP
With the opengl renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEXTURE_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEXTURE_UV_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the UV plane of an NV12 texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEXTURE_U_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the U plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEXTURE_V_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the V plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEXTURE_TARGET_NUMBER :
the GLenum for the texture target
.BR "" ( GL_TEXTURE_2D ,

.BR GL_TEXTURE_RECTANGLE_ARB ,
etc)
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEX_W_FLOAT :
the texture coordinate width of the texture (0\[char46]0 - 1\[char46]0)
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGL_TEX_H_FLOAT :
the texture coordinate height of the texture (0\[char46]0 - 1\[char46]0)
.PP
With the opengles2 renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGLES2_TEXTURE_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGLES2_TEXTURE_UV_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the UV plane of an NV12 texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGLES2_TEXTURE_U_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the U plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGLES2_TEXTURE_V_NUMBER :
the GLuint texture associated with the V plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_OPENGLES2_TEXTURE_TARGET_NUMBER :
the GLenum for the texture target
.BR "" ( GL_TEXTURE_2D ,

.BR GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES ,
etc)
.PP
With the gpu renderer:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_GPU_TEXTURE_POINTER :
the
.BR SDL_GPUTexture
associated with the texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_GPU_TEXTURE_UV_POINTER :
the
.BR SDL_GPUTexture
associated with the UV plane of an NV12 texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_GPU_TEXTURE_U_POINTER :
the
.BR SDL_GPUTexture
associated with the U plane of a YUV texture
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_TEXTURE_GPU_TEXTURE_V_POINTER :
the
.BR SDL_GPUTexture
associated with the V plane of a YUV texture

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I texture
the texture to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

